Day 38: The Cost of Love | Friday of the Fifth Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
Real love costs something.
Not because love demands pain —
but because love gives itself away.

Welcome to Day 38 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection invites you to contemplate the depth of Christ’s love — a love that holds nothing back, a love that lays down its life freely, willingly, completely. Jesus is the Good Shepherd who sees your wounds, your fears, your wandering, and chooses you again and again.

This spoken‑word devotional reminds you that sacrifice is not about punishment or proving your worth. It is about love — love that is patient, generous, forgiving, and willing to give even when it costs something. Jesus understands that kind of love. He lived it. He strengthens you to offer it.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why real love always costs something

How Jesus reveals the depth of His love through sacrifice

Why your quiet, hidden acts of love matter deeply

A prayer to love with courage and generosity

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Jesus, let this be love.”

